{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b0dbaff5-70a5-5e9f-a95b-81f86d9f4175",
    "name": "Livestock Registry Dashboard Service",
    "description": "Read-only aggregate API of the livestock registry, used by the OAN dashboards.\n\n- Every chart: `GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/charts/<chartId>` returns a JSON array of rows.\n- Filters (all optional, combined with AND) are included on each request but disabled; enable the ones you need. `all` or omitted means no filter.\n  - `region`, `zone`, `woreda`, `kebele`: P-codes, in any of the forms `ET04`, `region-ET04`, `REGION_ET04`.\n  - `recordState`: record status, case-insensitive. Without it, only ACTIVE records are counted (except `livestockByRecordState`).\n  - `state`: approval-workflow state (`DRAFT`, `KEBELE_APPROVED`, ..., `VERIFIED`).\n  - `species`: lookup key (`LIVESTOCK_SPECIES_CATTLE`), its last part (`CATTLE`) or the label.\n- Animal counts are head counts: a flock or set of hives recorded as one line counts its quantity.\n- The collection-level test checks status 200 and the exact response keys per chart. Example responses come from the service test fixture.\n\nSet `baseUrl` (collection variable, or the environment) to the service URL. The service has no authentication and is meant to be reachable on the private network only.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
